Aim
To demonstrate the Alpha-Beta pruning algorithm in a minimax decision-making process, optimizing game tree evaluations for two-player games like Tic-Tac-Toe.

Description
The code implements an Alpha-Beta pruning algorithm through the minimax function, which recursively evaluates optimal values for maximizing and minimizing players while pruning unnecessary branches based on Alpha and Beta thresholds.

The driver code initializes a set of leaf node values and calls the minimax function, printing the optimal score for the maximizing player. The values [3, 5, 6, 9, 1, 2, 0, -1] represent hypothetical outcomes for the leaf nodes.
